                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9ef125f4-3bd0-3b09-bded-7aea7ee29aa5",
                        "entry_id": "969eaa5f-9d17-399a-9e24-6d1950ae7d8d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To breathe (something) in; imbreathe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "ambitransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c440f7ab-e980-4802-88f3-2a5ce139d582",
                                "sense_id": "9ef125f4-3bd0-3b09-bded-7aea7ee29aa5",
                                "text": "She inbreathed sharply, then her eyes narrowed a trifle."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5e63af00-f055-3290-9c92-b50cf21a4a74",
                        "entry_id": "969eaa5f-9d17-399a-9e24-6d1950ae7d8d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To inspire (a person); communicate by inspiration; infuse by breathing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8000f9a2-e300-441e-b77a-ef7e8ce4c5c7",
                                "sense_id": "5e63af00-f055-3290-9c92-b50cf21a4a74",
                                "text": "And always remember that every mental power is a gift from Him; that actual power in life must be through Him only; and that mental gifts are not serviceable save as they are ever inbreathed by His own Spirit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2295af45-adea-4a70-a39b-85bd1b78a81c",
                                "sense_id": "5e63af00-f055-3290-9c92-b50cf21a4a74",
                                "text": "Both the scribe and the Scripture, both the man of God and the word of God were divinely inbreathed."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b6502af6-5b27-320f-8bd8-eacdf3b3cc82",
                        "entry_id": "969eaa5f-9d17-399a-9e24-6d1950ae7d8d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To draw in as breath; inhale; inspire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed1bc938-2926-4899-a1bc-4e5623dc3311",
                                "sense_id": "b6502af6-5b27-320f-8bd8-eacdf3b3cc82",
                                "text": "I had inbreathed their mystery and outbreathed it again as my own."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
